# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mayura Jewellers — environment
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value below:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env and .env.* are gitignored; this example file is the only one committed.
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing it — Vite reads env files at boot.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Web3Forms access key for the enquiry form on /contact.
#
# One-time setup:
#   1. Go to https://web3forms.com and enter mayurajewellers2019@gmail.com,
#      then press "Create Access Key". The key is emailed to that inbox.
#   2. Paste it below (a UUID, e.g. 1a2b3c4d-5e6f-7890-abcd-ef1234567890).
#   3. Add the same variable in Vercel under
#      Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production, Preview and
#      Development), then redeploy.
#
# The recipient address is bound to the key itself, so changing where enquiries
# land means issuing a new key — not editing any code.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle. That is
# expected here: a Web3Forms access key is a public, write-only identifier that
# can only post a message to the inbox it was issued for. Never put a real
# secret (API secret, database URL, password) behind a VITE_ prefix.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=cc6ff772-4305-46a5-905f-6b11ad150655
